  Q2. CPU Utilization Problem

Cause:
The processes repeatedly switch between Ready and Waiting states because they frequently perform I/O operations. The CPU remains idle while waiting for I/O to complete, resulting in low CPU utilization (30%).

Optimization:
Use multiprogramming or improve CPU scheduling so that when one process is waiting for I/O, another ready process is executed. This keeps the CPU busy and increases CPU utilization.

Final Answer:
Low CPU utilization is caused by frequent I/O waiting. Using multiprogramming and efficient CPU scheduling improves CPU utilization by executing another ready process whenever one process is waiting.

